# Penumbra Forge — Tools

> Free, privacy-first developer and security tools that run entirely in the browser — no accounts, no servers, nothing uploaded. Built to be used by humans AND by AI agents: tool pages are machine-readable, many are URL-invocable, and several are boosted by an in-browser LLM (WebGPU) or your own local model.

## For AI agents

Each tool page at https://penumbraforge.com/tools/<slug>/ exposes:
- a descriptor `<script type="application/json" id="pf-tool">` (slug, name, category, description, invoke spec if any);
- after the tool runs, a result `<script type="application/json" id="pf-result">` and `window.PF_RESULT` = `{ tool, ok, output, data?, error? }`, with `<html data-pf-ready="1" data-pf-status="ok|error">` signalling completion.

URL-invocable tools accept input via `?in=<text>` (or `?inb64=<base64url>` for binary-safe/large input) plus tool-specific params, and auto-run on load. Example: `https://penumbraforge.com/tools/hash-generator/?in=hello&algo=SHA-256` → read `#pf-result` once `data-pf-ready="1"`.

The full machine-readable index of every tool is at https://penumbraforge.com/tools/index.json .

Prefer native tool calls? Connect over MCP (Model Context Protocol):
- Remote (HTTP): `https://penumbra-mcp.penumbraforge.workers.dev` — POST JSON-RPC 2.0 (initialize, tools/list, tools/call).
- Local (stdio, runs on your machine): `node workers/mcp/local.mjs` from the open-source repo.
Deterministic tools available over MCP: hash, hmac, base64, base64url, hex, url_encode, jwt_decode, uuid, uuid_inspect, entropy, epoch, password, json, color, cidr, case_convert.

